L000575	\textit{Appendix I: Fiber's effective spring constant ---} The fiber's effective spring constant $k$ is measured by the static deflection of the fiber under its own weight. The values obtained range from 10 mN/m to 60 mN/m and are in good agreement with the cantilever beam equation for small deformations, $k = 3 E I / L^3$, with $I = \pi d_f^4 / 64$ the fiber's area moment of inertia, and $E \approx$~70~GPa its Young’s modulus. We considered only the linear regime (Hooke's law), which provides a good approximation with an average error of less than 1\% and a maximum error of less than 7\% in the worst-case scenario.
